an APK, or an XAPK for large apps made of several files - and install it directly on your phone, without Google Play and without a Google account."}],"$L27"],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}],"$L28","$L29","$L2a","$L2b","$L2c","$L2d","$L2e","$L2f","$L30","$L31","$L32","$L33"]]
23:["$","section",null,{"className":"space-y-3","id":"frequently-asked-questions","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"Frequently Asked Questions"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"divide-y divide-mist rounded-2xl border border-mist","children":[["$","details","Is APKPure safe?",{"className":"group p-4","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-ink","children":"Is APKPure safe?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/75","children":"Relatively safe compared with random APK sites, but not as safe as Google Play Store. APKPure checks developer signatures to make sure a file was not altered, but that check cannot detect an app that is malicious from its own developer, and it is not the same as Play Protect malware scanning. Use it carefully, and keep Play Protect switched on."}]]}],["$","details","Is APKPure safe now, after the 2021 incident?",{"className":"group p-4","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-ink","children":"Is APKPure safe now, after the 2021 incident?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/75","children":"The 2021 infection was in version 3.17.18 of the APKPure app. Kaspersky reported it on 8 April 2021, APKPure released the fix as version 3.17.19, and Kaspersky confirmed the new version was clean. The incident is history - it does not prove APKPure is infected today - but it also does not make the store safe forever. Treat every download with the same checks."}]]}],["$","details","Is APKPure legal?",{"className":"group p-4","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-ink","children":"Is APKPure legal?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/75","children":"Installing apps from outside Play Store - sideloading - is not a crime. Downloading a free app that is genuinely free is generally legal. Downloading a paid app for free is software piracy, whatever the platform. APKPure's policy is to refuse pirated apps, but with the volume it handles, some can slip through - so avoid any 'paid app for free' offer."}]]}],["$","details","What is the difference between APKPure and Google Play Store?",{"className":"group p-4","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-ink","children":"What is the difference between APKPure and Google Play Store?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/75","children":"Play Store reviews apps, verifies developer identities, and scans for malware with Play Protect, but generally only offers the latest version of apps released in your country. APKPure offers old versions and apps across regions through signature verification, but without Play Store's review depth or malware scanning."}]]}],["$","details","Why does Play Protect warn me when I install from APKPure?",{"className":"group p-4","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-ink","children":"Why does Play Protect warn me when I install from APKPure?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/75","children":"Because that is Android's standard policy for every app installed from outside Play Store - not a verdict that the file is malware. The warning reminds you the install skipped the official route: read it, check the app's permissions, and continue only if you trust the source."}]]}],["$","details","Does APKPure offer paid apps for free?",{"className":"group p-4","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-ink","children":"Does APKPure offer paid apps for free?"}],"$L34"]}],"$L35"]}]]}]
24:["$","section",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"Related Apps"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-1.5","children":[["$","li","tiktok",{"children":[["$","$L5",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-linkblue hover:underline","href":"/en/aplikasi/tiktok","children":"TikTok"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-ink/60","children":[" — ","TikTok Pte. Ltd."]}]]}],["$","li","whatsapp",{"children":[["$","$L5",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-linkblue hover:underline","href":"/en/aplikasi/whatsapp","children":"WhatsApp"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-ink/60","children":[" — ","Meta Platforms, Inc. (WhatsApp LLC)"]}]]}],["$","li","telegram",{"children":[["$","$L5",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-linkblue hover:underline","href":"/en/aplikasi/telegram","children":"Telegram"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-ink/60","children":[" — ","Telegram FZ-LLC"]}]]}]]}]]}]
25:["$","section",null,{"className":"space-y-3","id":"sources-and-further-reading","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"Sources and Further Reading"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-1.5","children":[["$","li","https://securelist.com/apkpure-android-app-store-infected/101845/",{"children":["$","a",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-linkblue hover:underline","href":"https://securelist.com/apkpure-android-app-store-infected/101845/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","children":"Kaspersky Securelist - Malicious code in APKPure app (9 April 2021)"}]}],["$","li","https://www.kaspersky.com/blog/infected-apkpure/39273/",{"children":["$","a",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-linkblue hover:underline","href":"https://www.kaspersky.com/blog/infected-apkpure/39273/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","children":"Kaspersky Daily - APKPure is not safe, distributes Trojans (9 April 2021)"}]}],["$","li","https://support.google.com/android/answer/2812853",{"children":["$","a",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-linkblue hover:underline","href":"https://support.google.com/android/answer/2812853","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","children":"Google Play Protect help - Use Google Play Protect to help keep your apps safe"}]}],["$","li","https://support.google.com/android/answer/9457058",{"children":["$","a",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-linkblue hover:underline","href":"https://support.google.com/android/answer/9457058","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","children":"Android Help - Download apps to your Android device"}]}],["$","li","https://apkpure.net/about.html",{"children":["$","a",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-linkblue hover:underline","href":"https://apkpure.net/about.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","children":"APKPure - About (apkpure.net)"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/60","children":"CekAPK provides educational information only. We do not guarantee the safety of any third-party APK file, and we have not independently tested APKPure's files."}]]}]
26:["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-ink/60","children":["English edition. The complete step-by-step version is on the ",["$","$L5",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-linkblue","href":"/panduan/apakah-apkpure-aman","children":"Indonesian guide page"}],"."]}]
27:["$","p","Installing from outside the offi",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Installing from outside the official store is called sideloading. Android allows it by design, but it asks for a special permission first - 'install unknown apps' - and Google Play Protect will show a warning. That warning is Android's standard policy for every install from outside Play Store, not a verdict that the file is a virus."}]
28:["$","section","How APKPure Works",{"className":"space-y-3","id":"how-apkpure-works","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"How APKPure Works"}],[["$","p","You search or browse for an app,",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"You search or browse for an app, pick a version, and download the APK or XAPK file. Android then asks you to allow installation from that source; once allowed, the app installs like any other. APKPure also offers older versions of apps, which Play Store generally does not, and apps that are not released in your country."}],["$","p","Before a file is listed, APKPure",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Before a file is listed, APKPure says it checks the file's digital signature against the original developer's signature, and that it scans files before publishing. Updates work the same way as the first install: you download the newer file from APKPure and install it. There is no Google account, no Play review, and no Play Protect check built into the store itself - the protection on your phone is whatever Android and Play Protect provide."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
29:["$","section","Is APKPure an Official Google Play Store?",{"className":"space-y-3","id":"is-apkpure-an-official-google-play-store","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"Is APKPure an Official Google Play Store?"}],[["$","p","No. APKPure is an independent st",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"No. APKPure is an independent store and is not affiliated with Google. Google Play Store is the official store on most Android phones - the one that comes with Google Mobile Services. APKPure is a separate company running its own catalogue, its own listing rules, and its own checks."}],["$","p","That distinction matters because",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"That distinction matters because the two stores offer different guarantees. Play Store reviews apps before publishing, verifies developer identities, and runs Play Protect malware scanning. APKPure relies mainly on signature verification and its own internal checks, without the same depth or transparency. Using APKPure is not using Google Play - it is using an alternative, with the trade-offs that come with it."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
2a:["$","section","The APKPure Security Incident of 2021",{"className":"space-y-3","id":"the-apkpure-security-incident-of-2021","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"The APKPure Security Incident of 2021"}],[["$","p","In April 2021, Kaspersky's resea",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"In April 2021, Kaspersky's researchers found malicious code inside the official APKPure app itself - version 3.17.18. The infection was most likely introduced through an advertising software kit (SDK) from an unverified source, a pattern Kaspersky compared to the earlier CamScanner incident, in which a developer's ad SDK turned out to be malicious."}],["$","p","When the infected app started, i",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"When the infected app started, it decrypted and ran a hidden payload. The payload collected information about the device and sent it to a command-and-control server, and depending on the server's response it could show ads when the phone was unlocked, open browser pages with ads again and again, and download further executable modules - including a Trojan closely related to the notorious Triada malware, which Kaspersky detects as HEUR:Trojan-Dropper.AndroidOS.Triada.ap. That Trojan could display and click ads, sign users up for paid subscriptions, and download other malware."}],["$","p","How bad it got depended on the p",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"How bad it got depended on the phone. On a reasonably recent Android version (Android 8 or newer), the main risks were paid subscriptions appearing out of nowhere and intrusive ads. On older phones running Android 6 or 7 without security updates, the malware could do far worse - including installing apps onto the system partition, where they survive even a factory reset, like the xHelper Trojan. The incident is a fact of history, and it is the single most important reason to treat any third-party store with caution - including this one."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
2b:["$","section","What Happened, Which Version Was Affected, and How It Was Fixed",{"className":"space-y-3","id":"what-happened-which-version-was-affected-and-how-it-was-fixed","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"What Happened, Which Version Was Affected, and How It Was Fixed"}],[["$","p","The affected version was APKPure",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"The affected version was APKPure 3.17.18. Kaspersky notified APKPure's developers on 8 April 2021. APKPure confirmed the problem the next day, and shortly afterwards released version 3.17.19. Its release notes said the update 'Fixed a potential security problem, making APKPure safer to use.' Kaspersky checked the new version and confirmed it: 'APKPure 3.17.19 doesn't contain the malicious component. It is safe to use.'"}],["$","p","That confirmation covers version",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"That confirmation covers version 3.17.19, in April 2021. It does not prove anything about other versions, and it does not mean the store is safe forever - it means the specific infection was found, disclosed, and removed quickly. If you ever used the APKPure app around that time, the advice then was to delete the infected version, install 3.17.19 or newer, and run a full scan of the device. The lesson that survives the incident is simpler: no platform is immune, not even the platform itself - so the safety of any store has to be checked continuously, not assumed once."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
2c:["$","section","Does APKPure Verify APK Signatures?",{"className":"space-y-3","id":"does-apkpure-verify-apk-signatures","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"Does APKPure Verify APK Signatures?"}],[["$","p","Yes - according to APKPure itsel",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Yes - according to APKPure itself. Every Android developer signs their app with a unique cryptographic key, a kind of digital fingerprint. APKPure states that it checks that the signature on each file it lists matches the original developer's signature before the file is published, and its own pages say every app goes through digital signature verification and that verified apps carry a Safety Badge."}],["$","p","That check is real protection, a",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"That check is real protection, and it is better than what most APK download sites offer - most check nothing at all. But its limit is widely misunderstood: a signature check only proves the file was not altered by someone else after the developer signed it. It answers the question 'was this file tampered with?', not the question 'is this app harmless?'. An app that is malicious from its own developer will pass signature verification, because its signature is genuinely the developer's."}],["$","p","The second question is answered ",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"The second question is answered by malware scanning and developer review - exactly what Google Play Protect and Play Store's review process do, and what APKPure does not do to the same standard. The good news is that Play Protect on your phone still scans apps installed from outside Play Store, so an APKPure user is not left entirely unprotected. The bad news is that a signature match is not a safety verdict - treat it as one check among several, never as a guarantee."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
2d:["$","section","The Risks of Downloading APKs From Third-Party Sources",{"className":"space-y-3","id":"the-risks-of-downloading-apks-from-third-party-sources","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"The Risks of Downloading APKs From Third-Party Sources"}],[["$","p","The first risk is malware in the",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"The first risk is malware in the file itself: spyware, adware, or banking Trojans hidden inside an app that looks ordinary. The second is repackaging: someone takes a genuine app, adds malicious code, and re-uploads it under the same name. Signature verification is designed to catch exactly this - but only if the store actually performs it, and only for files that pass through its listing process."}],["$","p","The third risk is outdated versi",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"The third risk is outdated versions. Old app versions can contain security holes that were fixed long ago, and an old version downloaded today may never be updated. The fourth is permission abuse: an app that asks for contacts, SMS, location, or accessibility access it does not need for its job, and then uses that access to read one-time codes or harvest data."}],["$","p","Then there are the risks that ha",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Then there are the risks that have nothing to do with code. Downloading a paid app for free is software piracy, whatever the platform - and the 'free paid app' offers that cluster around third-party stores are also where malware and lookalike domains concentrate. A file from a lookalike site, a comment link, or a chat message has none of the checks a real store applies, and there is no company to complain to if it damages your phone or empties an account."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
2e:["$","section","How to Check an APK Before You Install It",{"className":"space-y-3","id":"how-to-check-an-apk-before-you-install-it","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"How to Check an APK Before You Install It"}],[["$","p","No single check can guarantee an",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"No single check can guarantee an APK is safe. Use all of them together, and treat a failure of any one as a reason to stop. A clean antivirus scan does not guarantee an APK is completely safe - a scan only recognises threats it already knows, and new malware can pass undetected. Likewise, a matching developer signature proves the file is authentic, not that the app is harmless."}],["$","p","The limits matter as much as the",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"The limits matter as much as the checks. A signature match cannot catch malware written by the developer. A scan cannot catch malware nobody has seen yet. Permissions only tell you what an app asks for, not what it does with it. That is why the checklist works as a whole: each check closes a different gap, and none of them closes them all."}]],"$undefined",["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-2","children":[["$","li","Prefer Google Play or the develo",{"className":"flex gap-2.5 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-primary","aria-hidden":true,"children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Prefer Google Play or the developer's official website. If the app is there, there is no reason to get it anywhere else."}]]}],["$","li","Confirm the app name and the dev",{"className":"flex gap-2.5 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-primary","aria-hidden":true,"children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Confirm the app name and the developer identity. The developer of a banking app is the bank itself; a name that is almost right is a warning sign."}]]}],["$","li","Check the package name carefully",{"className":"flex gap-2.5 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-primary","aria-hidden":true,"children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Check the package name carefully. A genuine app keeps its official package name - a small change means a different app."}]]}],["$","li","Check whether the APK signature ",{"className":"flex gap-2.5 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-primary","aria-hidden":true,"children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Check whether the APK signature matches a trusted official version, where possible. A mismatch means the file was altered or comes from someone else."}]]}],["$","li","Review the requested permissions",{"className":"flex gap-2.5 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-primary","aria-hidden":true,"children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Review the requested permissions and question unrelated sensitive ones. A flashlight does not need your contacts; a wallpaper app does not need your SMS."}]]}],["$","li","Scan the APK with Google Play Pr",{"className":"flex gap-2.5 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-primary","aria-hidden":true,"children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Scan the APK with Google Play Protect. Play Protect can check apps installed from outside Play Store - keep it switched on and run a scan after installing."}]]}],["$","li","Do not ignore Android security w",{"className":"flex gap-2.5 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-primary","aria-hidden":true,"children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Do not ignore Android security warnings. A warning is not a verdict, but it is a reason to pause and check, not to tap through."}]]}],"$L36","$L37"]}],"$undefined"]}]
2f:["$","section","How to Use Google Play Protect",{"className":"space-y-3","id":"how-to-use-google-play-protect","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"How to Use Google Play Protect"}],[["$","p","Google Play Protect is Android's",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Google Play Protect is Android's built-in safety check. It is on by default, and Google recommends keeping it on. It checks apps from Play Store before you download them, and it also checks your device for harmful apps from other sources - including apps installed from APKPure. If it finds something harmful, it can warn you, disable the app, or remove it. It can also block an unverified app that asks for sensitive permissions commonly used in financial scams."}],["$","p","Play Protect can also check apps",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Play Protect can also check apps installed from sources outside Google Play - that is the point for an APKPure user. A scan result saying an app 'looks safe' is a good sign, not a guarantee; a warning is a reason to delete the app, not to argue with the warning."}]],"$undefined","$undefined",["$","ol",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","li","Open Google Play Store",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-mist p-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"grid h-9 w-9 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-primary font-bold text-white","aria-hidden":true,"children":1}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"block font-semibold text-ink","children":"Open Google Play Store"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 block text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/75","children":"Open the Play Store app on your Android phone."}]]}]]}],["$","li","Tap the profile icon",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-mist p-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"grid h-9 w-9 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-primary font-bold text-white","aria-hidden":true,"children":2}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"block font-semibold text-ink","children":"Tap the profile icon"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 block text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/75","children":"Tap your profile picture or initial at the top right of the screen."}]]}]]}],["$","li","Select Play Protect",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-mist p-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"grid h-9 w-9 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-primary font-bold text-white","aria-hidden":true,"children":3}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"block font-semibold text-ink","children":"Select Play Protect"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 block text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/75","children":"Tap Play Protect in the menu to open the safety overview."}]]}]]}],["$","li","Run a scan",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-mist p-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"grid h-9 w-9 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-primary font-bold text-white","aria-hidden":true,"children":4}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"block font-semibold text-ink","children":"Run a scan"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 block text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/75","children":"Tap Scan to check the apps on your device right now. Play Protect also scans automatically in the background."}]]}]]}],["$","li","Keep app scanning enabled",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-mist p-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"grid h-9 w-9 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-primary font-bold text-white","aria-hidden":true,"children":5}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"block font-semibold text-ink","children":"Keep app scanning enabled"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 block text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/75","children":"In Play Protect settings, keep 'Scan apps with Play Protect' switched on, so new installs - including sideloaded ones - are checked. Play Protect may also offer to send an unknown app to Google for a deeper check before you install it."}]]}]]}]]}]]}]
30:["$","section","Warning Signs That an APK May Be Dangerous",{"className":"space-y-3","id":"warning-signs-that-an-apk-may-be-dangerous","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"Warning Signs That an APK May Be Dangerous"}],[["$","p","A permission that has nothing to",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"A permission that has nothing to do with the app's job is the clearest warning: a calculator asking for contacts, a video player asking for SMS. A missing or unidentifiable developer is the second - a real app has a real company behind it, with a website and a history. A third is the source: a file offered in a chat message, a comment, or an ad, or on a domain that only resembles the real store's name."}],["$","p","Watch the promises too. 'Free Pr",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Watch the promises too. 'Free Premium forever', 'unlimited followers', or a paid app offered for free are not bargains - they are the bait that malware and piracy use. After installing, watch the phone itself: ads appearing on the home screen outside any app, a battery that suddenly drains, a phone that runs hot, or new permission requests that make no sense. Any one of these is a reason to uninstall the app and run a Play Protect scan."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
31:["$","section","APKPure vs Google Play Store",{"className":"space-y-3","id":"apkpure-vs-google-play-store","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"APKPure vs Google Play Store"}],[["$","p","Play Store wins on safety and ac",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Play Store wins on safety and accountability; APKPure wins on freedom of choice - old versions, apps outside your region, and no Google account. That freedom comes with a responsibility to check things yourself, because the store will not do it for you."}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-mist","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full min-w-[560px] border-collapse text-left text-sm","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-mist/60","children":[["$","th","",{"className":"border-b border-mist px-3 py-2 font-bold text-ink","children":""}],["$","th","APKPure",{"className":"border-b border-mist px-3 py-2 font-bold text-ink","children":"APKPure"}],["$","th","Google Play Store",{"className":"border-b border-mist px-3 py-2 font-bold text-ink","children":"Google Play Store"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"align-top","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Official store"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"No - independent third-party store"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Yes - Google's official store"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"align-top","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"App review before publishing"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Internal checks; signature verification (the company's own claim)"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Full review process, including developer identity checks"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"align-top","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Malware scanning"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Signature-focused; no Play Protect-level scanning in the store"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Play Protect scans apps before download and on the device"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"align-top","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Old app versions"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Available - a main reason people use it"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Generally only the latest version"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"align-top","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Region-locked apps"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Available across regions"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Only apps released in your country"}]]}],["$","tr","5",{"className":"align-top","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Google account needed"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"border-b border-mist/60 px-3 py-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"No"}],"$L38"]}],"$L39","$L3a"]}]]}]}],"$undefined","$undefined"]}]
32:["$","section","Safer Alternatives to APKPure",{"className":"space-y-3","id":"safer-alternatives-to-apkpure","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"Safer Alternatives to APKPure"}],[["$","p","The safest alternative is the on",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"The safest alternative is the one you already have: Google Play Store. It reviews apps, verifies developers, and runs Play Protect - and for the apps most people actually need, it is the whole answer. If an app is not on Play Store, the next safest source is the developer's own official website; many developers publish their APK there, signed with the same key as the Play version."}],["$","p","For open-source apps, F-Droid is",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"For open-source apps, F-Droid is a reputable catalogue that only lists free and open-source software, with reproducible builds for many apps - but it only covers open-source apps, not the commercial apps most people search for. Samsung's Galaxy Store is another official store, for Samsung phones. APKMirror is a widely used mirror that verifies signatures against Play Store versions, but it is still sideloading: the same checklist and the same Play Protect scan apply. Whatever the alternative, the rule does not change - the safest download is the one from the official store or the developer, and every step away from that needs more checking, not less."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
33:["$","section","Final Safety Recommendation",{"className":"space-y-3","id":"final-safety-recommendation","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"Final Safety Recommendation"}],[["$","p","So, is APKPure safe? No honest g",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"So, is APKPure safe? No honest guide can call it completely safe - and this one will not. It is safer than a random APK site because it checks developer signatures, and its 2021 infection was found, disclosed, and fixed within days. But signature checks cannot catch an app that is malicious from its own developer, the store does not scan like Play Protect does, and its own app was once the infection vector. That history does not prove APKPure is infected today - it proves no platform is immune."}],["$","p","Use Google Play Store first, and",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Use Google Play Store first, and the developer's official site second. If you still use APKPure, use only the official site, apkpure.com - never a lookalike domain or a link from a chat - keep Play Protect switched on, check the permissions before you install, and stay away from modified, cracked, or 'free paid app' files. An APK safety check is a habit, not a single scan: the store you choose matters, but what you check before tapping Install matters more."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
34:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/75","children":"According to its policy, no - APKPure says it refuses pirated apps. If you find a paid app offered for free under APKPure's name, treat it as piracy or a lookalike site, and do not download it."}]
35:["$","details","I already installed an app from APKPure - what should I check?",{"className":"group p-4","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-ink","children":"I already installed an app from APKPure - what should I check?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/75","children":"Check its permissions in Settings, run a Play Protect scan, and watch for strange behaviour such as aggressive ads, a draining battery, or odd new permission requests. If anything looks wrong, uninstall the app. Our Permission Checker can help you read an app's permissions from a screenshot if you are unsure."}]]}]
36:["$","li","Avoid modified, cracked, or susp",{"className":"flex gap-2.5 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-primary","aria-hidden":true,"children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Avoid modified, cracked, or suspiciously repackaged APKs. 'Mod', 'cracked', and 'free Premium' files are where malware and piracy meet."}]]}]
37:["$","li","Keep Android and your installed ",{"className":"flex gap-2.5 leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-primary","aria-hidden":true,"children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Keep Android and your installed apps updated. Security updates close the holes that older versions leave open."}]]}]
